{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"SnowplowEncoding","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"SnowplowEncoding"}],"title":"SnowplowEncoding","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Snowplow","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Snowplow"},{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") for a Snowplow pipeline in one call. It checks the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collector’s URL, the Iglu vendor and the app ID, and posts to the collector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" endpoint with a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". It splits each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch to the limits of Snowplow’s own mobile trackers (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"): 25","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events and 40,000 bytes a request, with a larger event, of up to 150,000 bytes, in a request of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its own. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A collector takes events from anyone who can reach it, so there is no key or secret, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination builds on every platform: an app sends to the collector directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SnowplowEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ the Iglu vendor the plan is exported under","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: snowplow)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":" for a collector URL that isn’t "},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", that has no host,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a user name, a query or a fragment, or that already ends in the endpoint; for a vendor Iglu"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t take; and for an empty app ID or one longer than 255 UTF-16 code units."}]},{"anchor":"Schemas-from-the-tracking-plan","type":"heading","text":"Schemas from the tracking plan","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event is a self-describing event: its data comes with the Iglu URI of the schema it must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"match, and Snowplow’s pipeline validates it against that schema before loading it. The URI is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"named after the event and its version, under the vendor the destination is given:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Version N of an event is SchemaVer "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and events always name it. Raising an event’s version"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a breaking change, which is SchemaVer’s MODEL. The export compares each event with the newest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schema of its version the registry holds, by what the two mean rather than their bytes, as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan’s own check does:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An event that hasn’t changed keeps its published file, and nothing is written.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A breaking change at the same version, such as a property made required, is refused: raise the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s version."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A compatible change, such as an optional property added, is an ADDITION. For Iglu Server the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"export writes it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-1"},{"type":"text","text":", then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-2"},{"type":"text","text":", each listing the earlier ones in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$supersedes"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow validates events naming "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":" against the newest, so a release already in users’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hands keeps validating. Superseding needs Iglu Server 0.11.0 or later and Enrich 3.8.0 or later."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A static repository doesn’t support it: it would validate those events against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":" alone,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so for one the export refuses the change, and the event needs a new version."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the registry from the plan with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan.writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iglu <vendor> server|static <registry-directory>"},{"type":"text","text":" command of the tracking plan’s executable, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"export-tracking-plan"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--iglu-vendor"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--iglu-registry"},{"type":"text","text":". Then publish it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"igluctl"},{"type":"text","text":" before the release that sends the events."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event name Iglu takes holds only ASCII letters, digits, "},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the version must be 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or more. The encoder skips every record of an event that breaks either rule, and logs a notice for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each such event of the plan when the destination is made. The export refuses such an event too."}]},{"anchor":"What-Snowplow-receives","type":"heading","text":"What Snowplow receives","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"payload_data"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-4 array of events, one per record. Every event has:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue"},{"type":"text","text":": a self-describing event, with its data in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue_pr"},{"type":"text","text":" as JSON text;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dtm"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ttm"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s timestamp in milliseconds, so Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"derived_tstamp"},{"type":"text","text":" is when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event was tracked;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"aid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the app ID; ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the platform; ","type":"text"},{"code":"tv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stm"},{"text":" is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, when the record has it, goes in ","type":"text"},{"code":"co","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"mobile_context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" 1-0-3","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(the operating system, Apple as the manufacturer, the device model, the network type and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"language) and ","type":"text"},{"code":"application","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" 1-0-0 (the app’s version and build). The platform is ","type":"text"},{"code":"mob","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a phone,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pad, watch or Vision Pro, ","type":"text"},{"code":"tv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for an Apple TV, ","type":"text"},{"code":"pc","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a Mac and ","type":"text"},{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a record with no device.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Only-the-session-identifies-a-record","type":"heading","text":"Only the session identifies a record","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, from the sessions enricher, is its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"},{"type":"text","text":", Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"domain_sessionid"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing else identifies it. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duid"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uid"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nuid"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tnuid"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent, no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity (its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"type":"text","text":" lasts across sessions), and no IDFV, IDFA or other device identifier. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent either. A record with no session, from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker without the sessions enricher, is sent without a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"},{"type":"text","text":"; a record a store recovered after a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relaunch keeps its session and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"},{"type":"text","text":". Snowplow’s mobile data models"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read a session from the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_session"},{"type":"text","text":" entity, so set the unified package’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"snowplow__session_identifiers"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[{\"schema\": \"atomic\", \"field\": \"domain_sessionid\"}]"},{"type":"text","text":" for these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector would give each device an identifier of its own: it sets an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sp"},{"type":"text","text":" cookie, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps and sends back, and records the request’s IP address. Every request carries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SP-Anonymous: *"},{"type":"text","text":", so the collector sets and reads no cookie, records "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network_userid"},{"type":"text","text":" as all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zeros, and records no IP address or forwarding header fields."}]},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","type":"heading","text":"Records left out","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name Iglu doesn’t take, or whose version is below 1;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 0 to 9999, which Snowplow’s enrichment fails;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes, which the smallest of a pipeline’s streams, SQS’s 192 kB,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"might not take with the request around it.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"What-the-collector-doesnt-report","type":"heading","text":"What the collector doesn’t report","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector answers 200 to every request it can read and validates nothing. Snowplow checks the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events later, in enrichment. An event whose data its schema rejects, whose schema the pipeline’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, or that is larger than the pipeline’s stream takes, becomes a failed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event: it is kept apart and never reaches the warehouse, though the destination counted it as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered. Publish each schema before the release that sends it, and watch the pipeline’s failed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events after a change to the plan. Snowplow’s resolver caches schemas, for 10 minutes by default,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a schema published after the first event that names it can still be missed for that long."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Snowplow doesn’t remove duplicates as events arrive. A record is sent more than once when a request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is retried after the collector stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each copy keeps its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"},{"text":", so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Snowplow’s data models, which deduplicate on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_id"},{"text":", count it once.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Snowplow receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/snowplowencoding"]}],"references":{"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"title":"snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appid:plan:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"snowplow","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"collector","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"URL","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"vendor","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"appID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowSetupError","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A10SetupErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"URLSessionTransport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"URLSessionTransport","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Encoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Snowplow collector at ","type":"text"},{"code":"collector","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as self-describing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events whose schemas are ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s under ","type":"text"},{"code":"vendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", from the app ","type":"text"},{"code":"appID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of ","type":"text"},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"topic"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan.","type":"text"}],"title":"SnowplowEncoding","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Snowplow’s trackers’ limits on one request, 25 events and 40,000 bytes of body, and an event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of up to 150,000 bytes in a request of its own.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder\/batchlimit","title":"batchLimit","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"